      <p>You can extract the <code>cluster-compare</code> plugin from a container image in the Red Hat container catalog and use it as a plugin to the <code>oc</code> command.</p>
      <h2 id="installing-cluster-compare_installing-cluster-compare-plugin" class="group scroll-mt-20">Installing the cluster-compare plugin<a href="#installing-cluster-compare_installing-cluster-compare-plugin" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Install the <code>cluster-compare</code> plugin to compare a reference configuration with a cluster configuration from a live cluster or <code>must-gather</code> data.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>You have installed the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>You installed <code>podman</code>.</li>
      <li>You have access to the Red Hat container catalog.</li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Log in to the Red Hat container catalog by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ podman login registry.redhat.io"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Create a container for the <code>cluster-compare</code> image by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ podman create --name cca registry.redhat.io/openshift4/kube-compare-artifacts-rhel9:latest"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Copy the <code>cluster-compare</code> plugin to a directory that is included in your <code>PATH</code> environment variable by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ podman cp cca:/usr/share/openshift/<arch>/kube-compare.<rhel_version> <directory_on_path>/kubectl-cluster_compare"} lang="terminal" />
      <ul>
      <li>
      <code>arch</code> is the architecture for your machine. Valid values are:
      <ul>
      <li><code>linux_amd64</code></li>
      <li><code>linux_arm64</code></li>
      <li><code>linux_ppc64le</code></li>
      <li><code>linux_s390x</code></li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li><code>&lt;rhel_version&gt;</code> is the version of RHEL on your machine. Valid values are <code>rhel8</code> or <code>rhel9</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;directory_on_path&gt;</code> is the path to a directory included in your <code>PATH</code> environment variable.</li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      View the help for the plugin by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc cluster-compare -h"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>The following is example output:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"Compare a known valid reference configuration and a set of specific cluster configuration CRs.\n\n...\n\nUsage:\n  compare -r <Reference File>\n\nExamples:\n  # Compare a known valid reference configuration with a live cluster:\n  kubectl cluster-compare -r ./reference/metadata.yaml\n\n ..."} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ul>
